<title>SLOVAKIA: SLOVAK FEB M2 UP 13.9 PCT YR/YR VS 15.5 PCT IN JAN.</title>
<headline>SLOVAK FEB M2 UP 13.9 PCT YR/YR VS 15.5 PCT IN JAN.</headline>
<dateline>BRATISLAVA 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The key Slovak money supply</p>
<p>aggregate, M2, rose 13.9 percent year-on-year in February 1997,</p>
<p>after a January increase of 15.5 percent year-on-year, the</p>
<p>National Bank of Slovakia (NBS) said in its February monetary</p>
<p>survey obtained by Reuters on Tuesday.</p>
<p> SLOVAK MONEY SUPPLY   FEB 1997  JAN 1997  FEB 1996  FY 1996</p>
<p> M2 overall (SKK bln)   406.5     405.0     356.9     416.9</p>
<p> pct change yr/yr	 +13.9     +15.5     +21.0     +15.7</p>
<p>Note. The NBS's full-year target for M2 expansion is 10.7</p>
<p>percent year-on-year. M2 measures currency, demand and time</p>
<p>deposits, savings deposits and foreign currency deposits.</p>
<p>-- Bratislava Newsroom, 42-7-521-8402</p>
</text>
